The Prophet of the Desert Sand

♫2360335142

He stood in the desert, a vision in black,  
With a high-collared jacket and abs on attack.  
The prophet of freedom, the king of Dubai,  
Who dips in ice water to wave us goodbye.  
“Your secrets are sacred! Your data is home!”  
Cried Pavel, while scraping your contact list dome.

He swore that his fortress was locked to the world,  
As the banners of “Privacy First” were unfurled.  
But don’t check the settings, and don’t peek inside,  
Where “end-to-end” secrets are easy to hide!  
The default is open, the cloud has the key,  
So the hackers and feds can read chats for a fee.

But who needs encryption when Pavel can flex  
In high-fashion photos that baffle and vex?  
We traded our safety for stickers of frogs,  
And left all our data to leak in the bogs,  
While the digital savior was striking a pose,  
With a filter to soften the bridge of his nose.

