But then came the blackout, the ultimate crash,  
That silenced the scammers and ruined the cash.  
The links of the t.me withered away,  
And left the whole internet gasping in gray.  
The loading wheels spun in a desperate dance,  
And the crypto-bros fell in a sorrowful trance.

No channel could broadcast, no bots could deliver,  
The “bulletproof” servers were starting to shiver.  
The drug-dealing channels, the leaks, and the spam,  
Were suddenly trapped in a giant traffic jam.  
And users screamed out in a panic of fright:  
“Where will I get my fake news for the night?”

For hours the network was silent and cold,  
As the myth of the “unbreakable” system unrolled.  
While Durov was probably combing his hair,  
His users were weeping in utter despair,  
Realizing their “safe” and “indestructible” space  
Was run on a server that fell on its face.

× × ×

Oh Pavel, the martyr, the free-speech crusader,  
Who turned in a flash to a cooperative trader!  
He flew to the Frenchmen, got cuffed at the gate,  
And decided compliance was better than fate.  
“I’ll give you the IPs, the logs, and the keys—  
Just let me go back to my yacht, if you please!”

So raise up a glass to the messenger grand,  
The least private highway in all of the land.  
With its spinning blue circle and high-fashion boss,  
Where your safety is always a total net loss!
